{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it burned to Cain greatly, and his face fell.</b> Cain and Abel knew the secret of the sacrifices and they brought an offering to the unique Name, blessed be He. Until now Scripture mentioned Elohim or YHWH Elohim, but now in the matter of the offering it mentioned the unique Name and said ״מנחה לה׳״ — 'an offering to YHWH.' And when they both brought offerings, the offering of Abel was accepted and that of Cain was not accepted. Then Cain had doubts concerning the matter of punishment and reward, and the Holy One, blessed be He, clarified the matter for him, that the entire world is governed according to punishment and reward. This is what He said to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:10.545434775Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}